{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff. The 11 entries of `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args` belong to this bug. Root-cause evidence (Windows JUnit 44681457334, probe run 44900309390, local macOS runs under core.autocrlf=true) is in this ticket's comments. Depends on transhuman-wounded-pangolin for one test (sub-cause 6).\n\n## Root cause (6 sub-causes; 2 in product code)\n1. **Product contract: `gitutil.run_git` / `_run_in_group` pipe str stdin in text mode.** On Windows Python rewrites each `\\n` as `\\r\\n`, so git receives CRLF. `hash-object --stdin` then hashes different bytes. No shipped caller is affected today: `reconciler/_ref_lock.py` already hashes bytes with `text=False`, and `_snapshot/delta_tree.py`'s checkout-index payload is NUL-separated. The fix makes `run_git`'s documented str-stdin contract platform-stable. The same translation makes `update-index --index-info` record nothing (probe run 44900309390), though no product caller does that today. Test: `test_run_git_wrapper::test_str_input_is_forwarded_to_stdin`.\n2. **Product: `llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py` writes `objects/info/alternates` in text mode.** The `\\r` stays in the path, the borrowed objects are not found, and `git reset --hard` exits 128. Tests: the 4 `test_plan_replay_tier2` materialize tests.\n3. **Checkout: 2 SHA-256-pinned vendored files carry no eol attribute.** Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so they check out CRLF and their pins fail. The files are `tests/external/live_jira_dc/pycontribs-jira-LICENSE.txt` and `.github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.json`. Tests: `test_jira_dc_harness_shape`, `test_bridge_provider_wrappers`, `test_reconcile_workflow_lint`.\n4. **Test harness: `_dc_fixtures.extract_store_snapshot` uses `git archive`, which applies core.autocrlf**, so extracted events come out CRLF. Test: `test_dc_store_copy_bounded_25e0` (this one reproduces on macOS too).\n5. **Test: `test_mcp_publisher_pin._verify` pipes the checksum line in text mode**, so `sha256sum` sees `'mcp-publisher.tar.gz'$'\\r'`.\n6. **Test: `test_reclaim_bridge_history::test_unrelated_remote_ref_movement_does_not_fail_dry_run` injects its ref through a `#!/bin/sh` file named `git` on PATH.** Windows never runs it, so the ref is never created and `rev-parse` exits 128. This is not line endings; it is the shell-stub problem transhuman-wounded-pangolin solves with `tests/_exe_stub.py`.\n\n## Approach\n1. `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py`: when `text=True` and `input_data` is str:\n   - Encode it with `_GIT_ENCODING`/`_GIT_ERRORS` (the codec text mode used) and run in binary mode with `check=False`.\n   - Decode stdout/stderr with the same codec and subprocess's universal-newline translation (`\\r\\n`→`\\n`, `\\r`→`\\n`), so returned text is identical on POSIX.\n   - Only then apply `check`, raising `CalledProcessError` with the decoded str. A `TimeoutExpired` gets its `output`/`stderr` decoded the same way.\n   - Apply the same in `_run_in_group`.\n   - The bytes-input contract and its TypeError are unchanged.\n   - `tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py::test_str_input_is_forwarded_to_stdin` writes its comparison file with `write_text`, which also writes CRLF on Windows. It will write `content.encode()` with `write_bytes`, so both sides hash the same LF bytes.\n2. `tier2.py`: open the alternates file with `newline=\"\\n\"`.\n3. `.gitattributes`: mark the 2 vendored pinned files `-text` so no checkout converts them. Their blobs are LF today (`ls-files --eol` shows `i/lf`), so the bytes are unchanged.\n4. `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py`: run `git -c core.autocrlf=false archive`.\n5. `tests/unit/test_mcp_publisher_pin.py`: pipe the checksum line as bytes.\n6. `test_reclaim_bridge_history.py`, `test_unrelated_remote_ref_movement_does_not_fail_dry_run`:\n   - Build the ls-remote shim with pangolin's `tests/_exe_stub.py` (a Python-body stub that Windows can run) instead of a `#!/bin/sh` file.\n   - Build the child environment as `{**os.environ, \"PATH\": os.pathsep.join([str(wrapper_dir), str(Path(git_executable).parent), os.environ.get(\"PATH\", \"\")]), ...test vars}`, so the stub dir is a real first PATH entry on every OS and Windows keeps SYSTEMROOT/PATHEXT. Today the `:`-joined PATH replaces the whole environment.\n   - This waits for pangolin's change on main.\n- New regression tests:\n  - `tests/unit/test_run_git_stdin_bytes.py`:\n    - With `subprocess.run` spied, a str `input_data` reaches subprocess as encoded bytes with `text` false. The decoded stdout is unchanged (including `\\r\\n`→`\\n`), and a failing `check=True` call raises `CalledProcessError` carrying str.\n    - With `subprocess.Popen` spied, the same holds for `_run_in_group` (reached through `run_git(timeout=...)`).\n  - In `test_plan_replay_tier2`, an assertion that the alternates file contains no `\\r`.\n- No config key, env var or flag.\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args`: remove each line whose test passes in the Windows validation run. If the file ends up empty, delete it and its `@` line in `.github/workflows/test.yml`.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py\n- .gitattributes\n- tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py\n- tests/unit/test_mcp_publisher_pin.py\n- tests/integration/test_reclaim_bridge_history.py\n- tests/unit/test_run_git_stdin_bytes.py\n- tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py\n- tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py\n- .github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args\n- .github/workflows/test.yml (only if the args file is deleted)\n\n## Testing\n- Pre-merge Windows validation on the exact fixed tree, with the lines removed: push `tmp/b4-neglectful-acceptable-gerbil`, dispatch `gh workflow run 294845723 --ref tmp/b4-neglectful-acceptable-gerbil`, and record the run id in a comment. Then delete the tmp branch.\n- AC1 evidence: the first scheduled `test.yml` run on main whose head contains the merge commit. Its run id goes in a comment before the close.\n- `make verify` through verify-slot.sh.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `crlf.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `crlf.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795275181339139001,"uuid":"6e3ff32f-25f5-4380-bc42-2fb7d260746e"}